{-
   An intrinsic whose declaration is not the shape its emitter depends on - `intrinsic/shape.h`.

   # resolver: ownership

   The check that did not exist before, and the reason it is worth its own fixture. A signature with
   no body *is* the signature: nothing duplicates it, the type checker reads it, and every call is
   checked against it. What the compiler adds is an emitter, and an emitter necessarily assumes
   things - that argument zero is a pointer, that the result is what it points at, that argument one
   arrives owned. Those assumptions were unwritten, and `attachIntrinsic` in the current resolver
   matches a name and checks nothing else.

   The live example is `Atomic.intoValue(->self: Atomic(a)) -> a`, whose declaration says the subject
   is handed over and whose expansion consumed nothing: the value stayed live, a second use was
   accepted, and the only thing keeping that from being a double release was that the content
   happened to be trivially copyable.

   Each declaration below is a plausible edit of a correct one, and each is reported at the
   declaration rather than at some call site that did nothing wrong.

   Two roles the prelude leaves unfilled, because `Core` imports `Native` and a role the prelude
   fills is one this file cannot claim a second time - `Reject.Roles.yana` beside this is where a
   second claim is the point.
-}

-- The contract. `hostWrite` stores its third argument into the host array, so the value has to
-- arrive owned - the array holds it afterwards, and the frame that owned it stops owing it a
-- teardown. The host family is the one the prelude never fills, which is what makes this row
-- claimable here; `exchange`, which used to stand here, is the prelude's now.
@builtin(hostWrite)
fn hostWriteShared(to: %a, at: Size, value: a) -> {}

-- The arity the role takes. `hostGrow` for `hostWrite`'s reason one line up: `mulHigh` used to
-- stand here and the prelude declares it now.
@builtin(hostGrow)
fn growThrice(items: %a, wide: Size, extra: Size) -> %a

fn main() -> I32 = 0
